//! @no_check
//! The function body's type must unify with the declared return type. Today
//! `check_module` infers the body but discards its type (inference.rs ~line 311),
//! so a mismatch is silently accepted. The @fail case pins that.
//!
//! IMPLEMENTER NOTE: the `pair`/`fst`/`wrap` helper bodies in tuples.rock /
//! app_types.rock are already real (`(x, x)`, `p.0`, `[x]`) and agree with their
//! declared returns, so enabling the check won't break them — just add the
//! `check_module` unify (`unify(body_ty, f.return_ty, f.span)`).

//- body_return_ok
fn f() -> int { 5 }
              //^ int

// body is string, declared return is int -> must fail once body-vs-return unifies.
// marker is what `5`... no — body is the string; in the buggy state the body type
// is ignored, so this type-checks; the marker on the body proves it's currently
// accepted (so @fail is RED now) and flips to a real error once the check lands.
//- body_return_mismatch @fail
fn f() -> int { "hi" }
              //^ string
